  "question": {
    "text": "The value of $f(0)$ so that the function $f(x)=\\frac{1-\\cos (1-\\cos \\mathrm{x})}{\\mathrm{x}^4}$ is continuous everywhere is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uJMKW",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0pxDx",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2JKeT",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{6}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tk6XA",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{8}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\text { Hints: } \\operatorname{Lim}_{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{1-\\cos (1-\\cos x)}{x^4}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Lim}_{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{2 \\sin ^2\\left(\\frac{2 \\sin ^2\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)}{2}\\right)}{x^4}=2 \\operatorname{Lim}_{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\sin ^2\\left(\\sin ^2\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\right)\\left(\\sin ^2\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\right)^2}{x^4\\left(\\sin ^2\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\right)^2}=2 \\operatorname{Lim}_{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\sin ^4\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^4 2^4}=\\frac{1}{2^3}=\\frac{1}{8}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
